<https://w3id.org/mobilitydcat-ap/releases/3.0.0/shacl/mdr-vocabularies#Dataset_MobilityTheme_CV> <http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl#description> "Values classify the theme of a mobility dataset using the Mobility Theme controlled vocabulary (https://w3id.org/mobilitydcat-ap/mobility-theme), which is organised in two hierarchy levels: data content category and data content sub-category. At least one value must come from this vocabulary; if no applicable concept exists, use the 'other' value (https://w3id.org/mobilitydcat-ap/mobility-theme/other). Values outside the vocabulary are tolerated."@en .
<https://w3id.org/mobilitydcat-ap/releases/3.0.0/shacl/mdr-vocabularies#Dataset_MobilityTheme_CV> <http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl#message> "mobilityTheme should include at least one concept from the Mobility Theme vocabulary; use 'other' if none applies."@en .
<https://w3id.org/mobilitydcat-ap/releases/3.0.0/shacl/mdr-vocabularies#Dataset_MobilityTheme_CV> <http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl#or> _:cb18d91513f425aa37881f7b8d5b738a2f2d47384ae42ad237bcc521881684e91d4 .
